From 96d46ead912db2d7963ad13c7764a82e92a274d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick <nekreshen@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:54:39 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] temporal AA: a title profile for games without guest markers

MCLA's temporal AA starts from its own guest markers and motion blur
shader. temporal_aa_anchor_ps and temporal_aa_camera let a title name
its frame instead: the scene is the draws on MSAA 2x surfaces (jittered,
tiles included), up to the first colour draw elsewhere; the camera's
view-projection is read from the constants of named vertex shaders in
the scene (the last frame's kept for camera motion); the pass runs
before the anchor pixel shader's draw, whose texture 0 is the scene,
with the frame's last depth resolve as the depth. A cut (the screen's
centre moving a third of the width) resets the history.

Metal: the depth's map to clip z comes from the scene's viewport (MCLA:
1 - depth), the scaler takes the scene's own colour format (8-bit after
a tone map, no auto exposure), and metal_taa_debug_vectors draws the
motion vectors in place of the result.

FIFA 19 (anchor C4F1B7FC, players' and props' view-projection): the pass
runs every match frame at 60 FPS; camera vectors check out (zero with a
still camera, an even field when it pans); the picture is softer than
without (grass texture smoothed).
